  "fields": {
    "responsibility": "One complete peer-pipe source owner across vector/string/u8 construction, shared FIFO/cursors, wait/reacquire, close publication and exception exit; generated C belongs to the same tested Scheme producer.",
    "retired": "Two per-endpoint mutexes guarding shared state; pipe constructors now publish one managed mutex before peer exposure. Ordinary four-argument calls retain a nonallocating optional sentinel and original body allocation order. Existing methods, public names, policies and C layouts retained; no permit table or new native namespace.",
    "validation": "Same-cache C23 native producer, one changed generated IO unit and50 unchanged artifacts; five real linker dependency recipes.12 native histories408 commands, replay/shrink13to1, six real read/write hook exceptions with GC/reentry, pinned processor1 transfers768 values, actual independent-pair and explicit-settings controls. Existing SFUN/frame/map multi-shot/old-module consumers pass; native slots12 and C word64.9 QNT cases,1000 bounded traces, TLC125 distinct states/depth17/empty queue. All34 original GSI IO and all34 compiled/executed under exact existing p1 compiler profile pass. Default GSC11/34 versus baseline14/34 with10 candidate-only/7 baseline-only names; both whole candidate attempts timeout120s versus exact baseline392/40896.841s. Broader introducedness unresolved, not declared passing.",
    "benefits": "A real baseline counterexample has two different guards for one shared FIFO domain. The common managed Scheme mutex restores actual exclusion and wait-predicate ownership across endpoints without binding to physical carrier threads. One fewer mutex record,104 source-accounted bytes per returned empty pair; still traceable and movable through existing GC.",
    "costs": "Peer directions contend on their actual shared state; optional dispatch and extra temporary roots remain. Final4096-pair body medians6.350ms\u21926.173ms are noisy, not stable speedup; peak footprint+16384 bytes. Gambit counter reduces851968, but2x movable accounting prevents calling it physical allocation saving. Frozen predecessor SFUN machine code adds one source call, not a second TLS lookup; repeat0/1/8 changes+4.985%/-0.732%/+0.698% versus earlier+2.065%/+1.217%/+2.680%, so stable timing attribution remains unresolved.",
    "process": "One whole four-path pipe responsibility, not isolated setters or bulk pending-prototype publication. Source catalogue stage5 only; historical foundation4/4 and independent SMP1/12 unchanged. Other49-queue owners remain separately audited; default compiler/whole GC modes stay blocked.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/pipe-domain.org#pipe-domain-owner",
    "models": "Strict OpenSysML SDK binds seven conditional obligations and three actual source maps to existing ASCENT current/missing/stale controls. New QNT only owns pipe-domain exclusion/wait/close, finite sent<=3 abstraction; no new Lean arithmetic/address law or duplicated GC state machine. Actual chunk arithmetic and native weak-memory/fairness remain source assumptions/older owners, not new model theorems.",
    "open": "Original default compiler and whole408 wall/source attribution, arbitrary IO continuation reentry, asynchronous owner death, duplex throughput/peak and whole Gerbil/release remain unqualified. Different pairs have independent locks; this is not a global IO lock or a claim that the whole scheduling/SMP stage is solved."
  },
